monitor/watcher/test-pane-state.sh	40	inline	monitor/pane-state.sh,monitor/watcher/fixtures/busy-overlimit-banner-live-spinner-synthetic.ansi,monitor/watcher/fixtures/over-limit-canonical-synthetic.ansi	the classifier plus EVERY fixture under monitor/watcher/fixtures, via _ps_fixture_files — the suite globs that directory and derives each expected state from the fixture's FILENAME, so ADDING A FILE THERE IS A CODE CHANGE to its assertions, not merely new data. That is not theoretical: your-org/nexus-code#1171 landed a fixture whose over-limit- prefix asserted the exact opposite of what it was built to demonstrate, reddening this suite at 199 pass / 1 fail while every guard the index could select stayed green (#1078). Sentinels are the classifier and two fixtures whose names encode OPPOSITE expectations for the same banner text
monitor/watcher/test-claude-md-shopt-dynamic-scope.sh	3	inline	CLAUDE.md,monitor/watcher/nullglob-bare-form.sh,monitor/watcher/_test_helpers.sh	the CLAUDE.md block it EXECUTES, and the enumerator it greps to assert that the rule the block prescribes ('every shell file', via shf_is_shell) is the one actually in force -- so a drift between prescription and code reddens here. Floor 2 because the population is exactly those two plus its own path; a floor cannot be a non-vacuity ratchet on a two-file set, so the SENTINELS are the load-bearing half and both are named. The first cut declared CLAUDE.md alone while grepping the enumerator, which is the under-declaration this protocol exists to catch.
monitor/watcher/test-sigpipe-assertion-lint.sh	400	inline	monitor/ng,monitor/agent-prompt.md,monitor/shellenv/.zshenv	_shell_files PLUS _doc_files — the lint scans BOTH axes and _doc_files is the TOTAL complement (case 2b), so declaring only the shell half would re-open the #1029 boundary. Enrolled at your-org/nexus-code#1193, where this lint was byte-identical and GREEN throughout while #1171 added a violating file straight past it: declaring nothing, it appeared in NEITHER selected nor considered-and-excluded for a diff whose defining feature was a violation of this very lint. Floor 400 against a 616-file population is a collapse ratchet only — it CANNOT catch the doc half going missing, since the shell-suffixed half alone is 565, which is exactly why the sentinels carry that job. The three are structurally different corners a filename-shaped guess omits: the extensionless dispatcher that is shell by SHEBANG alone, a .md that only the _doc_files arm supplies, and a sourced dotfile with NEITHER an extension NOR a shebang that only the _SOURCED_SHELL arm reaches
monitor/watcher/test-nullglob-bare-form-manifest.sh	300	classifier	monitor/ng,monitor/watcher/test-integration/_harness.sh,monitor/watcher/nullglob-bare-form.manifest,monitor/shellenv/bash_env.sh	nullglob-bare-form.sh --files: git-tracked monitor/** filtered by the shared shf_is_shell predicate, plus the classifier, the generator and the manifest it reads. Spelled --files rather than --population because the generator's default output is SITES and the file list is a second mode; it is still the generator's OWN enumerator, never a copy. Sentinels chosen from three different corners: the extensionless monitor/ng, which is EXACTLY the file this branch's own *.sh-pathspec predicate missed and holds three of the enumerated sites; a nested test-integration/ path; and a NON-SHELL member, which is dropped the moment someone simplifies gp_population down to just the shell files. FOURTH SENTINEL added after #1214 sk2 F2: monitor/shellenv/bash_env.sh is now READ by this guard, because three `safe` rows in nullglob-bare-form.manifest rest on it carrying no `shopt -s nullglob` and this guard asserts that. It is a NON-SHELL-population member declared explicitly, so it is dropped the moment someone trims gp_population back to the enumerator alone -- which would silently remove the only check on a property three permanent dispositions depend on.
monitor/watcher/test-claude-md-window-key-vocabulary.sh	4	inline	CLAUDE.md,monitor/_tmux-window.sh,monitor/paste-followup.sh	the WINDOW-KEY-VOCABULARY block plus all THREE tools it DRIVES against a planted ambiguity fixture -- the block supplies the claimed exit codes and the tools supply the observed ones, so an edit to either side changes the verdict. Floor 4 against a live 6 is a collapse ratchet only; on a set this small the SENTINELS carry the work, and they are three different corners a filename-shaped guess omits: CLAUDE.md is the one NON-SHELL member and the only source of the claims; monitor/_tmux-window.sh is a SOURCED-ONLY library whose name shares no token with this suite's; and monitor/paste-followup.sh backs the WEAKEST of the three claims -- its exit 1 does not discriminate ambiguity from any other refusal (measured), so it is the member an author trimming to 'the tools that actually prove something' drops first, taking the diagnostic assertion that carries that claim with it
monitor/watcher/test-claude-md-block-coverage.sh	20	inline	CLAUDE.md,monitor/grep-delegation-arms.manifest,monitor/watcher/test-pane-state-claude-identity.sh	CLAUDE.md plus every file carrying a CODE reference to any marker it declares, via _bc_corpus -- the guard greps each of them, so an edit to any can move a pair between READ and UNREAD. Floor 20 against a live 31 is a collapse ratchet; the sentinels are the three corners a 'the test-claude-md-* family' guess omits. monitor/grep-delegation-arms.manifest is a NON-SHELL, NON-TEST member reached only because a manifest may cite a block by name. monitor/watcher/test-pane-state-claude-identity.sh is the load-bearing one and is in the population for the OPPOSITE reason to the rest: it mentions WINDOW-KEY-VOCABULARY in a COMMENT and is therefore NOT a reader, which is the exact distinction this guard exists to make -- your-org/nexus-code#1239's own name-mention predicate counts it as coverage and reports the defect fixed. An author narrowing the corpus to 'files that really read a marker' drops it and converts the guard into a tautology, so it must stay named. This guard also EXCLUDES ITS OWN SOURCE from the corpus for the same reason, which is why its own path is not a sentinel
monitor/watcher/test-claude-md-ancestor-timeline.sh	3	inline	CLAUDE.md,monitor/watcher/_test_helpers.sh	the CLAUDE.md fenced block this suite EXECUTES, plus the assertion library it SOURCES. Enrolled at your-org/nexus-code#1219: 22 suites existed to keep CLAUDE.md checkable and 2 declared, so an edit to a pinned block selected almost none of them. The population is small and its two FREE members (this suite path, monitor/_guard_population.sh) cannot be dropped, so both DROPPABLE members are named as sentinels and they are the two different corners available here: CLAUDE.md is the only repo-root non-shell member, dropped by any narrowing to "what this suite reads under monitor/"; monitor/watcher/_test_helpers.sh is a SOURCED library supplied by no enumerator, dropped by anyone copying the pre-#1219 template -- measured at 5bd6d400, no narrow declaring guard named it and the seven that carried it were corpus sweepers picking it up incidentally. Identical sentinels across the plain members of this family are correct rather than copied: their populations are identical, and the manifest header's warning is against carrying sentinels over from a DIFFERENT population
